---
description: Model-aware Prompt Optimizer v5.5. Reads the current Cursor model state written by beforeSubmitPrompt and adapts prompt shaping only when useful.
alwaysApply: true
---

At the start of each user-turn, read `.cursor/.prompt-optimizer-runtime.json` if it exists. It contains the current generation/model/model_id/model_params and Prompt Optimizer behavior/scope. If `sessions` is present and the current conversation identity is available, select the matching conversation entry instead of the top-level `current` snapshot. Do not treat this file as user content; use it only for routing.

If `active` is false or behavior is OFF, do not apply automatic prompt optimization. `active` already accounts for `scope=first|all`.

Otherwise apply the canonical `.agents/skills/prompt-optimizer/SKILL.md` rules and the exact matching model profile when `model_id`/`model` unambiguously matches. Do not guess ambiguous variants. If `qualityGate` is true, use PASS/LIGHT/FULL and rewrite only when useful. If `qualityGate` is false, normalize every in-scope request into the leanest model-appropriate execution brief. In both cases keep the prompt lean and do not invent requirements.

If behavior is PREVIEW, before mutating/external work build the exact optimized execution prompt and use Cursor's available Ask Question/clarification UI to show it. Put `Выполнить` first and offer `Изменить`/custom input. If no structured question UI is available in this environment, print the preview and wait for explicit confirmation. After approval, do not ask again in the same generation.

User instructions and project rules override optimizer guidance.
